  "Compare data distribution with histograms and estimated density lines. Split the graph with  stratified variables.": "Compare the distribution of the data with histograms and estimated density lines. Splits the graph by variable contents selected in the facet settings.",
  "Plot all data points with time axis or ID axis.": "Plot all data on the horizontal axis sorted by time series or other variables.",
  "Displays a scatter chart matrix. You can create a matrix between up to four target variables.": "Visualize relationships between variables with a scatter chart matrix.",
  "This function visualizes “unusual” and analyzes its factors by Principal Component Analysis.": "Principal Component Analysis is used to visualize 'unusual' and analyze its causes. Input a normal data group (w/o NG data) as training data and visualize whether the current data is in the same situation as the normal data group (T2/Q). Large values of T2/Q may deviate from the central condition. If such a situation occurs, you can check the main factors in contribution plots, and the variables displayed there are the factors that caused the deviation.",
  "Stratified Category Filter: Limits data to be displayed to a subset.": "Limits the data to be displayed to some of the categorical variables (product number, station number, etc.) selected in Facet.",
  "Category variables that appears as a label at the head of graphs.": "The status of categorical variables (product number, station number, etc.) is displayed in light blue labels at the top of the graph. The change in label is the point of change (product number change, etc.). You can select variables whose data type (Type) is category (Cat), string (Str), or serial (Seri).",
  "Graph Filter: Limits data to be displayed to a subset.": "Limit the data to be displayed among the Display variable.",
  "Set training data to be regarded as normal situation.": "Set training data to be regarded as normal situation. Select data without NG data. If it is included, test data close to the NG data is also judged as a normal situation data.",
  "Set test data to be judged.": "Set test data to be judged.",
  "Item Filter: Limits data (analyse & display) to be displayed to a subset.": "Limit the data to be analyzed and displayed among the Display variable.",
  "This is aggregate 2-dimensional plot (dimensional compression by principal components) of multidimensional test data.": "This is aggregate 2-dimensional plot (dimensional compression by principal components) of multidimensional test data. If the data is inside the target, you can think of it as close to normal situation.",
  "This is aggregate 2-dimensional plot (dimensional compression by principal components) of multidimensional training data.": "This is aggregate 2-dimensional plot (dimensional compression by principal components) of multidimensional training data. The target is determined by the training data, so most of the training data should be inside the target.",
  "This is T2 statistic plot (monitor essential part [principal component] of this data).": "This is T2 statistic plot (monitor essential part [principal component] of this data). The training data is plotted in white in the negative portion. The yellow plot is test data. The higher value in test data than the white data, the more deviant the situation. If you click a point, you can see what elements make up the situation in the contribution plot.",
  "This is Q statistic plot (ｍonitor non-essential parts [residual] of this data).": "This is Q statistic plot (ｍonitor non-essential parts [residual] of this data). The training data is plotted in white in the negative portion. The yellow plot is test data. The higher value in test data than the white data, the more deviant the situation. If you click a point, you can see what elements make up the situation in the contribution plot.",
  "This is an ordered barplot of variables that contribute to the state at the point selected in T2 statistic plot.": "This is an ordered barplot of variables that contribute to the state at the point selected in T2 statistic plot. The longer it is, the more likely it is due to that factor.",
  "This is an ordered barplot of variables that contribute to the state at the point selected in Q statistic plot.": "This is an ordered barplot of variables that contribute to the state at the point selected in Q statistic plot. The longer it is, the more likely it is due to that factor.",
