  "Thin data shown": "Since the number of data points drawn in one graph is 12,000 or more, the data points on the 100%% plot are thinned out to a maximum of 12,000 points.<br>If you want to see the data without thinning out the data, set the target period so that the number of data is less than 12,000 points.",
  "Stratify by term (Cyclic)": "Stratify by term (Cyclic)",
  "Facet": "Facet",
  "Category expansion is performed to divide the graph using the data of the selected item.": "Divide the graph by the contents of the selected variable. You can select items whose data type (Type) is category (Cat) or string (Str). \nIf you select only Lv1 or Lv2, the graph will be divided by the contents of selected variable.\nIf you select both Lv1 and Lv2, the graph will be divided according to the combination of the contents of the two selected variables.\n\n*RLP, AgP, and ScP pages, you can select Div in addition to Lv1 and Lv2. The roles of Div are as follows\n・RLP,AgP: The selected variable is used on the horizontal axis, and the contents of the variable are aggregated by contents.\n・ScP: The graph is divided in the same way as Lv1 and Lv2, but the divided graphs are arranged vertically for Lv1 and Lv2, and horizontally for Div.\n・WfP: Waveforms are drawn for each value of the selected variable.",
