  "Precision": "Prediction",
  "Recall": "Recall",
  "ROC-AUC": "ROC-AUC",
  "PR-AUC": "PR-AUC",
  "Accuracy description": "Number of correct predictions made divided by the total number of data.\nIf the number of positive labels is extremely smaller than the negative labels (example: OK/NG data), consider using precision/recall/PR-AUC.",
  "Precision description": "Higher value indicates the fewer false alarms (false positives).\nNumber of correct predictions made divided by the number of positive predictions.",
  "Recall description": "Higher value indicates the fewer overlooks of the positive labels.\nNumber of correct predictions made divided by the number of positive labels.",
  "ROC-AUC description": "Use when the number of positive/negative labels is balanced.\nHigher value indicates the higher performance to both labels.\nThe area under the curve when plotting the relationship between the false positive rate and the true positive rate while changing the threshold.",
  "PR-AUC description": "Use when the number of positive labels is extremely smaller than the negative labels.\nHigher value indicates the higher performance of predicting the positive labels.\nThe area under the curve when plotting the relationship between the precision and the recall while changing the threshold.",
  "Serial series": "Others",
  "Mode hover msg": "Select the EMD (Earth Mover's Distance) calculation mode that indicates the degree of distribution variation.",
  "Drift hover msg": "When calculating the degree of distribution variation (EMD) for each distribution, the top distribution is used as the reference.",
  "Diff hover msg": "When calculating the degree of distribution variation (EMD) for each distribution, the previous distribution is used as the reference.",
  "Both hover msg": "Display the results calculated in both modes of Drift and Diff.",
  "Contour hover msg": "Draws a scatter plot with contour showing the central portion of the distribution. If the number of data points drawn in one scatter plot is 10,000 or more, scatter plot with contour is shown to omit the data points drawn on the plot.",
  "Heatmap hover msg": "The background color is changed according to the magnitude of the correlation coefficient. Among the selected variables, combinations of variables with larger absolute values of correlation coefficients are displayed in brighter colors.",
