  "Error Msg Common": "Error is occurring!!",
  "Filter search box hover msg": "General Search Options\n    ・OR Search: Including multiple words(spaces are treated as characters) separated by '|'.  (ex. A|B C → AX, B CX, AXB C)\n    ・Range Search: Including numbers in the range specified by '[-]'. (ex. [98-101] → X098, X099, X100)\nRegular Expression: Specify the format of serial etc. in detail.",
  "First": "First",
  "Last": "Last",
  "Duplicate serial": "Duplicate serial",
  "Duplicate serial hover message": "You can select the record to display when there are duplicate records in the item set for 'As Link ID' on the process setting page.\nWhen data linking between several processes, duplicate serials are forcibly linked with the latest date & time record.",
  "Remove duplicated records message": "Excluded `x` duplicate records.",
  "P duplicate hover message": "Number of duplicate serials (percentage)",
  "You can filter categorical data used for graph drawing.": "You can filter categorical data used for graph drawing.",
  "TourSelectTargetVar": "Select a process and then select some variables that you would like to visualize. You can select additional process by clicking the + button on the upper right.BREAK_LINEBREAK_LINEYou can also set variables for label plots and facets.BREAK_LINE",
  "TourSelectTargetVarDesc": "BREAK_LINEYou can show the description of the words with underlines by pointing the words with mouse pointer for a second.",
  "TourSelectTargetPeriod": "If \"Date range\" is selected (default), you can specify the datetime range of the data with start/end datetime.BREAK_LINEYou can select \"Latest\" to visualize data from the current time up to a specified time in the past (e.g. past 24H). In addition, selecting \"Auto Update\" will refresh the graph periodically.",
  "TourSelectTargetPeriodDatePicker": "Clicking on the textbox will show datetime selector. You can specify the datetime range with this selector, or by typing directly with the keyboard.",
  "TourFindData": "No problem. Clicking the \"Data Finder\" button, you can access data finder, which you can find the time range of the stored data.",
  "TourWithDatafinder": "With the data finder, you can select a datetime range while seeing when and how much data is being imported.BREAK_LINEBREAK_LINEIf data exists, the corresponding cell is displayed in blue; the greater the amount of data, the brighter the blue. The existence of this data refers to the data for the process selected first in the step \"Select Display variable\" or the process specified as theSPAN_TAG\"Start point\"SPAN_END_TAG",
  "TourUseFilter": "If you had already configured a filter setting in A_TAG\"Filter Config\"A_END_TAG page, you can specify those filters here (e.g. part no, test  lag, etc.). BREAK_LINEBREAK_LINEThe Analysis Platform also has a function \"On demand filter\", which you can filter the data after the visualization. The on demand filter do not require prior configuration. Press Filter button FILTER_ICON after you had visualized the data.",
  "TourCleansing": "Please select the data cleansing methods you wish to apply. (multiple selection is possible) BREAK_LINEBREAK_LINE",
  "TourShowGraph": "The basic setup is finished. Most of the settings done in this tour are common among most of the visualization. BREAK_LINEBREAK_LINEFinally, press the \"Display Graph\" button and wait a few moments for the graph to be drawn.",
  "TourFinish": "Thank you for completing this tour. BREAK_LINEBREAK_LINEMany useful functions, including on-demand filters, are also implemented on the screen after visualization. Manipulations on the graph will never destroy the imported data, so lets start manipulating the graph and analyze the data from various angles.",
