  "Japanese name is duplicated": "Japanese name is duplicated",
  "Local name is duplicated": "Local name is duplicated",
  "DataFinderHoverMsg": "Target period for which there is data for the process selected at the Start point (or the first process) is displayed in light blue. You can check when the data is collected from each unit: yearly [Year] ⇔ monthly [Month] ⇔ (daily [Week]). Please input the target range by using the information. The first click specifies the starting point (From), and the second click specifies the ending point (To). Press [Set] to enter the last selected date and time into the target period.",
  "ZeroVarianceTitle": "A variable whose variance is 0 (all data are the same).",
  "NARateTitle": "Missing data rate",
  "Division number Hover AgP": "Enter the number of distributions (Number of Divisions) to display. Please enter an integer (1 ≦ int ≦ 1000)",
  "Window length Hover": "Enter the time width for calculating one distribution. Please enter a number between 0.01 (=36 seconds) and less than 20,000 (=833 days). If it is equal to the step size, evaluate all data without overlap (recommended setting). If it is larger than the step size, data overlap will occur (effective when there is little data. However, since some of the same data is evaluated, there is a concern that changes may become slow). If the value is smaller than the step size, data will not overlap and some data will not be evaluated (effective when there is a large number of data. However, not recommended as some data will not be evaluated). \ne.g.) 1 week = 168h, 30 days = 720h, a half year = 4320h, one year = 8760h",
  "Window length Hover AgP": "Enter the time width for calculating one plot or summary result. Please enter a number between 0.01 (=36 seconds) and less than 20,000 (=833 days). If it is equal to the step size, evaluate all data without overlap (recommended setting). If it is larger than the step size, data overlap will occur (effective when there is little data. However, since some of the same data is evaluated, there is a concern that changes may become slow). If the value is smaller than the step size, data will not overlap and some data will not be evaluated (effective when there is a large number of data. However, not recommended as some data will not be evaluated). \ne.g.) 1 week = 168h, 30 days = 720h, a half year = 4320h, one year = 8760h",
  "Window length Hover ScP": "Enter the time width for one graph. Please enter a number between 0.01 (36 seconds) and 20,000 (=833 days). If it is equal to the step size, evaluate all data without overlap (recommended setting). If it is larger than the step size, data overlap will occur (effective when there is little data. However, since some of the same data is evaluated, there is a concern that changes may become slow). If the value is smaller than the step size, data will not overlap and some data will not be evaluated (effective when there is a large number of data. However, not recommended as some data will not be evaluated). \ne.g.) 1 week = 168h, 30 days = 720h, a half year = 4320h, one year = 8760h",
  "Division number Hover ScP": "Enter the number of graphs (number of divisions) to display. Please enter an integer less than or equal to 7 when Facet is enabled, and less than or equal to 49 when Facet is disabled.",
  "Interval Hover": "Enter the date and time interval when displaying the distribution by date and time. Please enter a number with an absolute value of 0.01 (36 seconds) or more and 720 (=30 days) or less. You can set the period backwards by entering a negative value. \ne.g.) 1 week = 168h, 30 days = 720h, a half year = 4320h, one year = 8760h",
  "Interval Hover AgP": "Enter the date and time interval when displaying plot or summary results by date and time. Please enter a number with an absolute value of 0.01 (36 seconds) or more and 720 (=30 days) or less. You can set the period backwards by entering a negative value. \ne.g.) 1 week = 168h, 30 days = 720h, a half year = 4320h, one year = 8760h",
  "Interval Hover ScP": "Enter the date and time interval when displaying the graph by date and time. Please enter a number with an absolute value of 0.01 (36 seconds) or more and 720 (=30 days) or less. You can set the period backwards by entering a negative value. \ne.g.) 1 week = 168h, 30 days = 720h, a half year = 4320h, one year = 8760h",
  "Divide by category hover msg AgP RLP": "The variables selected for the Div are used on the horizontal axis, and are aggregated or aggregated by type of variable content.",
  "Divide by category hover msg ScP": "The graph is divided according to the content of the variable selected in Div and arranged horizontally.",
  "Stratify by variables hover msg StP": "The graph is divided according to the type of variable selected for Lv1 or Lv2 of Facet settings. If you select both Lv1/Lv2, the graph will be divided by the combination of the contents of the two selected variables.",
  "Divide by term (Cyclic) hover msg": "Decomposes the graph in periodic time",
  "Divide by term (Direct) hover msg": "Directly enter the time period you want to visualize and break down the graph for each input time period.",
  "Divide by data number (Cyclic) hover msg": "Break down the graph by the number of input data.",
  "Divide by calender (Cyclic) hover msg": "Break down the scale of the horizontal axis by year, fiscal year, half year, quarter, month, week, day, and hour.",
  "Skip line hover msg": "This item is set when the column name does not exist in the first row. You can enter a value between 0 and 100. \nIf nothing is entered, the data will be loaded using the first row as column names. \nIf 0, column names will be automatically generated. Also, if nothing is entered and there are many numbers in the first line, 0 will be entered automatically. \nIf it is 1 or more, the data will be skipped to the row number of the entered value, and the data will be read using the next row as the column name.",
  "Num rows hover msg": "Limits the number of lines to be read. No input or 0 will read all lines, a positive number will read only the specified number of lines.",
  "Transpose hover msg": "Transpose the data, which swaps the rows and columns.",
